<title>USA: AGA says U.S. weekly natgas stocks rose 27 bcf.</title>
<headline>AGA says U.S. weekly natgas stocks rose 27 bcf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Gas Association estimates of U.S. working gas in storage in billion cubic feet</p>
<p>(bcf):		    11/01/96  10/25/96  Net Chg  Pct Full(6)</p>
<p> Producing Reg. (1)	  670     660	+10     74</p>
<p> Consuming Reg. East (2)  1721    1699	+22     96</p>
<p> Consuming Reg. West (3)   334     339	- 5     69</p>
<p> Total U.S.		   2725    2698	+27     86</p>
<p>Notes: (1) Incl Texas, Okla., Kansas, N.Mexico, Arkansas, Louisiana, and Miss. (2) Incl states east of Miss. River less Miss., plus Iowa, Neb and Missouri (3) Incl states west of the Miss. River less producing region and Iowa, Neb and Missouri.  </p>
<p>Survey sample and full working gas estimates</p>
<p> -			 Survey Sample   Est. Full Work-    Yr-Ago</p>
<p> -			 Size--Pct (4)   ing Gas--BCF (5)   Week</p>
<p> Producing Region	    71		    908	   812</p>
<p> Consuming Region East     95		   1790	  1723</p>
<p> Consuming Region West     96		    482	   423</p>
<p> Total U.S.		    88		   3180	  2958</p>
<p>Notes: (4) Ratio of max WG vol. to est. of highest WG in storage in past 2 yrs (EIA).(5) Highest WG level by state added to give regional and national levels (EIA).(6) Regional and total vols divided by est.full regional and total vols.</p>
</text>
